1
00:00:13,677 --> 00:00:15,441
O-Con.

2
00:00:16,657 --> 00:00:18,361
Yes? Yes?

3
00:00:18,989 --> 00:00:20,700
Let's get married.

4
00:00:21,725 --> 00:00:23,569
Yes.

5
00:00:25,333 --> 00:00:26,505
What?

6
00:00:26,505 --> 00:00:28,917
Let's get married.

7
00:00:28,917 --> 00:00:30,657
Huh?

8
00:00:31,417 --> 00:00:32,608
Kekkon?

9
00:00:32,608 --> 00:00:33,933
Marriage.

10
00:00:34,765 --> 00:00:38,281
Wait, by "kekkon" you mean
the dark blood at a crime scene

11
00:00:38,281 --> 00:00:40,181
that splashes everywhere?
[*"Bloodstain" sounds like]

12
00:00:40,181 --> 00:00:43,353
That'd be a bloodstain.
[*"marriage" in Japanese]

13
00:00:45,585 --> 00:00:47,729
Oh, sorry. Please, continue.

14
00:00:47,729 --> 00:00:51,025
- No, no, no, no.
- You go get changed too, Mr. Hirose.

15
00:00:51,025 --> 00:00:53,100
Go get changed. Hello?

16
00:00:53,100 --> 00:00:55,517
Thank you for your continued support.

17
00:00:58,293 --> 00:01:01,633
- Why get married?
- What do you mean, 'why'?

18
00:01:01,633 --> 00:01:03,277
Because I love you, O-Con.

19
00:01:03,277 --> 00:01:05,867
L-L-Lo... That 'love'...

20
00:01:05,867 --> 00:01:08,838
Is it like loving Berry, or loving Tuesla?

21
00:01:08,838 --> 00:01:11,773
- That same kind of...
- No, no, no.

22
00:01:11,773 --> 00:01:16,489
The heart-squeezing kind,
the stomach-twisting kind.

23
00:01:16,489 --> 00:01:21,685
Stomach-twisting...
So it's that kind of love.

24
00:01:21,685 --> 00:01:25,829
I mean, I was away from you for a few days,

25
00:01:25,829 --> 00:01:29,965
but then we had this miraculous reunion.

26
00:01:29,965 --> 00:01:34,937
I just didn't want to be apart.
So I figured, "Marriage, then."

27
00:01:34,937 --> 00:01:39,241
"You must hold on tight to what you love."

28
00:01:39,241 --> 00:01:41,577
My grandma just said that.

29
00:01:41,577 --> 00:01:43,017
It's just too sudden.

30
00:01:43,017 --> 00:01:45,861
Oh, so you mean you need time to think?

31
00:01:45,861 --> 00:01:47,841
Sure, think about it. Go ahead.

32
00:01:47,841 --> 00:01:49,297
- Ten, nine, eight...
- Wait, hold on!

33
00:01:49,297 --> 00:01:51,237
- Seven, six, five...
- What am I supposed to think? Wait!

34
00:01:51,237 --> 00:01:52,621
- Four, three, two...
- Wait, wait, wait! What?

35
00:01:52,621 --> 00:01:53,769
- One, zero.
- What?

36
00:01:53,769 --> 00:01:55,633
- Let's get married.
- No way!

37
00:01:57,565 --> 00:01:59,369
- Oh.
- What do you mean, 'oh'?

38
00:01:59,369 --> 00:02:01,401
I should be the one saying 'oh'!

39
00:02:01,401 --> 00:02:03,745
This is huge! This is huge!

40
00:02:03,745 --> 00:02:05,933
Well, compared to a marriage proposal,
I'm not sure which is bigger.

41
00:02:05,933 --> 00:02:07,125
I guess it's a toss-up, but still.

42
00:02:07,125 --> 00:02:08,466
- But a marriage proposal is still...
- What happened?

43
00:02:08,466 --> 00:02:11,289
The merch shop just called.

44
00:02:11,289 --> 00:02:13,817
They said that inquiries
about Tuesla are flooding in!

45
00:02:13,817 --> 00:02:17,597
- Huh?
- They want to place an additional order!

46
00:02:17,597 --> 00:02:22,393
- Oh!
- Oh!

47
00:02:22,393 --> 00:02:24,401
We need to get things organized quickly.

48
00:02:24,401 --> 00:02:27,073
- I'm off.
- Right. Let's get organized.

49
00:02:27,073 --> 00:02:29,113
Let's get everything organized.

50
00:02:29,113 --> 00:02:32,845
So, your homework. An answer.

51
00:02:32,845 --> 00:02:35,257
Home...

52
00:02:35,257 --> 00:02:37,573
Why?

53
00:02:37,573 --> 00:02:39,833
I already told you, no way.

54
00:02:41,269 --> 00:02:44,357
Fifty Tueslas, right? Thank you.

55
00:02:44,357 --> 00:02:45,847
However, we're currently

56
00:02:45,847 --> 00:02:49,337
- unable to keep up with production.
- Please, do what you can.

57
00:02:49,337 --> 00:02:52,117
- Hey, are you okay?
- I'm so sorry.

58
00:02:52,117 --> 00:02:54,273
- Here, propolis is good for your throat.
- Thank you.

59
00:02:54,273 --> 00:02:57,166
- Yes. Thank you.
- Here's some propolis for you guys too.

60
00:02:57,961 --> 00:03:00,985
- Proposal...
- Thank you.

61
00:03:00,985 --> 00:03:03,901
Oh, be careful. That's really heavy.
[*"Really" sounds like]

62
00:03:03,901 --> 00:03:05,766
'Marriage' heavy?
[*"marriage" in Japanese]

63
00:03:12,189 --> 00:03:14,525
We now have over 100,000 followers
on Chirp Wave!

64
00:03:14,525 --> 00:03:16,941
- What?
- What? Amazing!

65
00:03:16,941 --> 00:03:20,417
- Wow! Amazing!
- Wow, amazing!

66
00:03:20,417 --> 00:03:22,137
[Just looking at it is healing.]
Come on!

67
00:03:22,137 --> 00:03:23,137
[A slow-burn kind of cuteness.]
Congratulations.

68
00:03:23,137 --> 00:03:25,074
[Cute? I watched the video.]
Thanks. Amazing.

69
00:03:25,074 --> 00:03:26,804
[He's just a guy who's not a mooch, lol.]
100,000.

70
00:03:27,583 --> 00:03:30,493
- Wow.
- Amazing. 100,000.

71
00:03:33,865 --> 00:03:36,073
Quick! Someone, take his phone away!

72
00:03:36,073 --> 00:03:37,081
What are you doing?

73
00:03:37,081 --> 00:03:39,781
Mr. Seo was replying to negative comments!

74
00:03:40,841 --> 00:03:42,561
Geez.

75
00:03:43,625 --> 00:03:45,029
It was just a reply.

76
00:03:45,029 --> 00:03:48,066
"Oh, yeah, yeah. Saying something
different from everyone else,

77
00:03:48,066 --> 00:03:50,861
like you want to be special, huh?"

78
00:03:50,861 --> 00:03:52,817
"Finding your place in the world,
good for you."

79
00:03:52,817 --> 00:03:55,873
That's not just a reply. It's a provocation.

80
00:03:55,873 --> 00:03:58,629
From today on, I'll handle the updates
on the official secret account.

81
00:03:58,629 --> 00:04:00,637
Please stop looking at social media, Mr. Seo.

82
00:04:00,637 --> 00:04:02,766
Whatever you do, don't look at it.

83
00:04:04,441 --> 00:04:05,825
Okay.

84
00:04:05,825 --> 00:04:09,385
Because there will be
even worse comments in the future.

85
00:04:09,385 --> 00:04:12,433
Of course, that's kind of proof
that you're getting popular.

86
00:04:12,433 --> 00:04:16,066
It's a side effect of having
more people who like you.

87
00:04:19,505 --> 00:04:21,566
Hello, this is Kusakabe.

88
00:04:23,561 --> 00:04:25,325
Huh?

89
00:04:25,325 --> 00:04:29,600
T-T-The Ministry of Economy,
Trade and Industry?

90
00:04:30,341 --> 00:04:32,473
[2035 Animal Expo]
Tuesla as an ambassador?

91
00:04:32,473 --> 00:04:37,373
Yes, for the Animal Expo held in 2035.

92
00:04:37,373 --> 00:04:40,021
If you could lend your support
as the bid ambassador...

93
00:04:40,021 --> 00:04:42,217
We'll do it. Please let us do it.

94
00:04:42,217 --> 00:04:45,821
Tuesla can be a help to
everyone on the world stage.

95
00:04:45,821 --> 00:04:48,113
That would be so wonderful.

96
00:04:48,113 --> 00:04:51,209
Then, once again, thank you for your support.

97
00:04:51,209 --> 00:04:53,341
Thank you for your support as well.

98
00:04:53,997 --> 00:04:57,385
Also, since this is a public project,

99
00:04:57,385 --> 00:05:00,557
the public scrutiny will be intense.

100
00:05:00,557 --> 00:05:03,585
Please be especially careful to
avoid any problematic behavior.

101
00:05:04,381 --> 00:05:06,177
Problematic behavior?

102
00:05:06,177 --> 00:05:07,381
[It's gotten so popular all of a sudden, lol.
What's so good about it?]

103
00:05:07,381 --> 00:05:09,381
[No, I just don't get the cuteness.]

104
00:05:09,381 --> 00:05:14,229
Oh, no, you're looking at social media again.
We already said you can't do that.

105
00:05:16,117 --> 00:05:17,537
Please rest assured.

106
00:05:17,537 --> 00:05:22,209
Our company's motto is
'zero problematic behavior'.

107
00:05:22,209 --> 00:05:25,153
At today's regular meeting,
the major shareholders are also...

108
00:05:25,153 --> 00:05:28,821
Due to the recent worsening performance,
the stock price has plummeted!

109
00:05:28,821 --> 00:05:32,437
Starting with Harsh Review Molco's scandal,
then Docchicchi's failure,

110
00:05:32,437 --> 00:05:34,349
and then the blunder at
the Character Grand Prix,

111
00:05:34,349 --> 00:05:37,201
everything you do just backfires, doesn't it?

112
00:05:37,201 --> 00:05:41,089
You're the cause of all of this,
aren't you, Mr. Omishima?

113
00:05:41,089 --> 00:05:45,137
If this continues, we'll have no choice
but to ask you to resign.

114
00:05:45,137 --> 00:05:48,825
I apologize for causing concern.

115
00:05:50,433 --> 00:05:52,593
But please rest assured.

116
00:05:52,593 --> 00:05:55,205
The next move is already in motion.

117
00:05:58,273 --> 00:06:03,261
I've made many wrong decisions.

118
00:06:04,369 --> 00:06:07,345
The feelings of those who support us,

119
00:06:07,345 --> 00:06:11,700
and even the feelings of the characters,
I've neglected them.

120
00:06:12,689 --> 00:06:16,413
So I think it's only natural
that I face the consequences.

121
00:06:16,413 --> 00:06:18,241
However,

122
00:06:19,161 --> 00:06:21,721
Molco hasn't done anything wrong.

123
00:06:23,301 --> 00:06:25,277
Omishima.

124
00:06:27,653 --> 00:06:29,773
[Emergency Press Conference]
<i>I couldn't</i>

125
00:06:29,773 --> 00:06:32,300
[by Merry President Omishima]
<i>make Molco happy.</i>

126
00:06:33,349 --> 00:06:35,177
So...

127
00:06:36,609 --> 00:06:40,133
in order to make Molco happy,

128
00:06:40,133 --> 00:06:42,657
I've made the decision to part ways.

129
00:06:42,657 --> 00:06:45,541
Part ways? With what?

130
00:06:45,541 --> 00:06:48,666
What do you mean by 'part ways'?

131
00:06:49,693 --> 00:06:52,193
We, Merry,

132
00:06:52,193 --> 00:06:55,633
will transfer the rights to Cynical Molco.

133
00:06:57,209 --> 00:06:58,555
Huh?

134
00:06:58,555 --> 00:07:00,255
Huh?

135
00:07:10,433 --> 00:07:11,721
[Episode 8]

136
00:07:11,721 --> 00:07:15,805
I can't believe they're
transferring Molco's rights.

137
00:07:15,805 --> 00:07:17,269
If you give up the rights to a character,

138
00:07:17,269 --> 00:07:20,301
you won't get the profits
if it becomes a hit later.

139
00:07:20,301 --> 00:07:21,973
Even more importantly, the character...

140
00:07:21,973 --> 00:07:24,981
You don't know how it'll be treated.

141
00:07:25,761 --> 00:07:27,849
What do you mean, 'how'?

142
00:07:27,849 --> 00:07:32,941
In cases like this, the rights
go to the highest bidder.

143
00:07:32,941 --> 00:07:36,277
And if it's a shady company,

144
00:07:36,277 --> 00:07:40,177
they might use the character to
advertise shady pots or something.

145
00:07:41,217 --> 00:07:43,389
Well, to be honest,

146
00:07:43,389 --> 00:07:46,877
I don't really care what
happens to Cynical Molco.

147
00:07:46,877 --> 00:07:49,637
<i>Means so much.</i>

148
00:07:49,637 --> 00:07:52,581
<i>Ever since Mr. Omishima became president,</i>

149
00:07:52,581 --> 00:07:54,721
<i>Merry has made a V-shaped recovery.</i>

150
00:07:54,721 --> 00:07:59,866
Well, but, you know... How do I put it...

151
00:08:01,077 --> 00:08:03,317
But look, Mr. Omishima is saying

152
00:08:03,317 --> 00:08:05,941
[Announcing the transfer]
that it's for Molco's sake.

153
00:08:05,941 --> 00:08:06,941
[of Cynical Molco's rights]
Look.

154
00:08:06,941 --> 00:08:08,689
- See these tears.
- <i>I cherish it more than anyone.</i>

155
00:08:08,689 --> 00:08:11,239
I don't think this is a lie.

156
00:08:12,661 --> 00:08:14,453
This is an act.

157
00:08:14,453 --> 00:08:15,557
An act?

158
00:08:15,557 --> 00:08:18,001
Like, those tears that look like
they're about to fall but don't?

159
00:08:18,001 --> 00:08:19,305
- <i>Excuse me.</i>
- Yes.

160
00:08:19,305 --> 00:08:21,857
At the previous celebration for
Molco's movie adaptation,

161
00:08:21,857 --> 00:08:24,457
a drunk Mr. Omishima muttered

162
00:08:24,457 --> 00:08:28,029
that he was into acting
and was good at crying scenes.

163
00:08:28,029 --> 00:08:30,081
Really? That's news to me.

164
00:08:30,081 --> 00:08:35,789
What I heard was a drunk Mr. Omishima
muttering that he was into gospel music.

165
00:08:35,789 --> 00:08:40,125
- What's true about Mr. Omishima...
- Lies, lies. All lies.

166
00:08:40,125 --> 00:08:43,200
That's the kind of guy he is. This too.

167
00:08:44,109 --> 00:08:49,825
We won't choose the winning bidder
based on the size of the offer.

168
00:08:49,825 --> 00:08:55,493
We'll choose based on
how much they love Molco here,

169
00:08:55,493 --> 00:09:00,066
and what they'll do to make Molco happy.

170
00:09:02,185 --> 00:09:04,766
As for Molco's new partner,

171
00:09:05,777 --> 00:09:10,800
I'd like to select them through
a live broadcast open competition.

172
00:09:11,425 --> 00:09:14,065
An open competition, of all things.

173
00:09:14,065 --> 00:09:16,125
Is that like a reality show?

174
00:09:16,125 --> 00:09:19,489
I mean, someone who's genuinely
worried about Cynical Molco

175
00:09:19,489 --> 00:09:21,581
would never do something like this.

176
00:09:21,581 --> 00:09:25,233
He's full of lies. He's Mr. Lie-mishima.

177
00:09:25,233 --> 00:09:28,249
Looking at this, opinions on social media
are split right down the middle.

178
00:09:28,249 --> 00:09:30,553
Some say he's just selling it for money

179
00:09:30,553 --> 00:09:33,305
and are telling him not to make it
sound like a heartwarming story,

180
00:09:33,305 --> 00:09:37,745
while others say he's admirable
for sacrificing so much for Molco.

181
00:09:37,745 --> 00:09:39,013
Indeed.

182
00:09:39,013 --> 00:09:44,281
The loss from giving up Cynical Molco,
the backbone of Merry, is real.

183
00:09:44,281 --> 00:09:48,233
And yet he says he wants Molco to be happy.

184
00:09:48,233 --> 00:09:50,600
He's doing this very skillfully.

185
00:09:58,529 --> 00:10:03,313
[Labravo's Bravo Journey]
The shareholders contacted us just now.

186
00:10:03,313 --> 00:10:08,989
They're asking if it's really okay
to let go of Cynical Molco.

187
00:10:08,989 --> 00:10:10,913
Then, I have a question as well.

188
00:10:10,913 --> 00:10:12,661
Who was it that brought Merry back

189
00:10:12,661 --> 00:10:16,117
from the brink of bankruptcy
in a V-shaped recovery?

190
00:10:16,117 --> 00:10:17,889
It was you, Mr. Omishima.

191
00:10:17,889 --> 00:10:22,129
Then, who is causing
the stock price to plummet now?

192
00:10:24,649 --> 00:10:26,701
Don't hold back.

193
00:10:28,373 --> 00:10:30,801
- It's you, Mr. Omishima.
- That's right.

194
00:10:30,801 --> 00:10:34,341
In other words, the company Merry
is entirely dependent on me.

195
00:10:34,341 --> 00:10:39,269
What's important isn't the characters,
but Takumi Omishima.

196
00:10:39,269 --> 00:10:40,989
Indeed.

197
00:10:40,989 --> 00:10:45,613
With this open competition,
I plan to restore Merry's cohesion

198
00:10:45,613 --> 00:10:48,797
and create a new hit product.

199
00:10:48,797 --> 00:10:53,009
Cynical Molco is just material for that.

200
00:10:53,009 --> 00:10:55,081
Sorry to keep you waiting.

201
00:10:55,081 --> 00:10:56,213
Mr. Morita.

202
00:10:56,213 --> 00:10:58,897
[Trend Up TV Producer]
Actually, there's something I'd like to do.

203
00:10:58,897 --> 00:11:02,573
[Tatsuyuki Morita]
Oh, what is it? Let's hype it up.

204
00:11:03,249 --> 00:11:07,709
There's someone I'd like to have
participate in this open competition.

205
00:11:08,385 --> 00:11:09,518
[Exclusive Interview with]
Are there any conditions

206
00:11:09,518 --> 00:11:11,213
[Merry President Takumi Omishima]
for this transfer of rights?

207
00:11:11,213 --> 00:11:13,341
[In-depth look at the highly anticipated]
No, there aren't any conditions.

208
00:11:13,341 --> 00:11:15,565
[open competition]
If I find a person whom I think is right,

209
00:11:15,565 --> 00:11:18,945
I'll hand over all rights
to them unconditionally.

210
00:11:18,945 --> 00:11:21,233
What do you mean, 'all rights'?

211
00:11:22,245 --> 00:11:27,257
That means everything,
including this production process.

212
00:11:27,257 --> 00:11:28,805
I see.

213
00:11:28,805 --> 00:11:32,461
And the judge will be you, Mr. Omishima?

214
00:11:32,461 --> 00:11:37,801
Look, here, here, here!
Full Tummy Molco is clearly shown!

215
00:11:41,041 --> 00:11:42,173
This is...

216
00:11:42,173 --> 00:11:46,037
Full Tummy Molco is being used
as a character to advertise shady pots.

217
00:11:46,037 --> 00:11:47,465
[Apply here]

218
00:11:47,465 --> 00:11:49,685
I'll take it back!

219
00:11:49,685 --> 00:11:53,097
- No, wait... Don't!
- Hey!

220
00:11:53,097 --> 00:11:56,093
- Let go!
- If you act like that on a live broadcast,

221
00:11:56,093 --> 00:11:57,969
it'll immediately be problematic behavior!

222
00:11:57,969 --> 00:12:00,188
[2035 Animal Expo, Tutu-Tuesla]
And if that happens, our dream

223
00:12:00,188 --> 00:12:02,749
of bringing Tuesla to everyone
could be cut short!

224
00:12:02,749 --> 00:12:05,061
So you're going to
make Molco sell shady pots?

225
00:12:05,061 --> 00:12:07,305
The pot thing is just an example!

226
00:12:07,305 --> 00:12:09,233
I mean!

227
00:12:10,245 --> 00:12:12,193
In the first place,

228
00:12:12,193 --> 00:12:18,825
this kind of selling off... is just sad.

229
00:12:18,825 --> 00:12:20,949
I kind of get it too.

230
00:12:20,949 --> 00:12:25,273
I know there are times
when rights and stuff are a thing.

231
00:12:25,273 --> 00:12:27,333
But somehow,

232
00:12:28,097 --> 00:12:30,829
I just can't help but think that it's sad.

233
00:12:30,829 --> 00:12:35,166
Full Tummy Molco, Cynical Molco.

234
00:12:40,805 --> 00:12:42,517
Let's enter.

235
00:12:43,385 --> 00:12:47,077
The open competition.
Let's definitely enter it.

236
00:12:47,077 --> 00:12:48,763
- But...
- With Seo Design's

237
00:12:48,763 --> 00:12:51,029
overflowing love for its characters,

238
00:12:51,029 --> 00:12:54,800
let's go save Full Tummy Molco,
Cynical Molco, and everyone else!

239
00:12:57,673 --> 00:13:00,400
That's right. Let's enter.

240
00:13:02,113 --> 00:13:05,625
Yes, let's enter.

241
00:13:05,625 --> 00:13:09,601
- O-Con, let's get married...
- But only on one condition...

242
00:13:09,601 --> 00:13:11,500
Which is, no scandals allowed.

243
