And next, the final candidate will appear.

484
00:27:58,017 --> 00:27:59,973
[Designer, Merry Co., Ltd.]
Please come forward.

485
00:27:59,973 --> 00:28:01,973
[Rena Kawasaki]

486
00:28:03,529 --> 00:28:04,741
Why?

487
00:28:04,741 --> 00:28:09,545
The final candidate is,
surprisingly, Rena Kawasaki!

488
00:28:09,545 --> 00:28:13,425
She is the current chief designer at Merry,

489
00:28:13,425 --> 00:28:17,093
and also the main designer of Cynical Molco.

490
00:28:17,857 --> 00:28:21,869
It seems that Mr. Omishima
didn't know about her participation.

491
00:28:25,489 --> 00:28:31,409
Ms. Mondo always said
that characters are not tools.

492
00:28:31,409 --> 00:28:33,933
They are alive.

493
00:28:34,681 --> 00:28:38,201
I oppose Mr. Omishima's

494
00:28:38,201 --> 00:28:42,729
transfer of Cynical Molco's rights.

495
00:28:42,729 --> 00:28:45,825
If I can obtain its rights,

496
00:28:45,825 --> 00:28:48,537
I will separate all decision-making
authority regarding Molco

497
00:28:48,537 --> 00:28:55,141
from Mr. Omishima and management,
and return it to the creators.

498
00:28:55,141 --> 00:28:56,231
[That red dress suits her too well!
The successor to Mondo-ism!]

499
00:28:56,231 --> 00:28:57,285
[Now this is a character designer!
We've been waiting for someone like this!]

500
00:28:57,285 --> 00:28:58,413
[It's crazy that even
the president didn't know!]

501
00:28:58,413 --> 00:28:59,413
[I kind of want to root for her. Go for it!]

502
00:28:59,413 --> 00:29:01,381
[Carry the next generation of Merry!]

503
00:29:01,381 --> 00:29:02,757
[Kitchen Sakoda]
<i>And that concludes</i>

504
00:29:02,757 --> 00:29:04,641
<i>the company introductions
from the eight candidates,</i>

505
00:29:04,641 --> 00:29:07,621
selected after strict examination.

506
00:29:07,621 --> 00:29:11,333
It's great that
Tuesla became a hit, isn't it?

507
00:29:13,137 --> 00:29:14,649
Thanks.

508
00:29:14,649 --> 00:29:19,925
When you were with us, you were
pretty much unknown, right, Mr. Seo?

509
00:29:19,925 --> 00:29:22,821
Okay, commercial break.
We'll now be taking a short break.

510
00:29:22,821 --> 00:29:26,097
- Thank you.
- Yes. Let's take a break.

511
00:29:26,097 --> 00:29:28,165
Well, then.

512
00:29:28,165 --> 00:29:30,233
- Good work.
- Good work.

513
00:29:39,469 --> 00:29:45,341
Wow, prosciutto and melon,
so elegantly done. Truly a prince.

514
00:29:46,217 --> 00:29:48,001
It's delicious.

515
00:29:48,001 --> 00:29:50,233
The Completion Plan is a huge success!

516
00:29:50,233 --> 00:29:54,245
But Rena's appearance was a bit unexpected.

517
00:29:54,245 --> 00:29:59,449
And in fact, she got the most buzz online.

518
00:30:07,593 --> 00:30:10,869
Hey, hey, how was it? How was it?

519
00:30:10,869 --> 00:30:13,941
Great! Great performance!

520
00:30:13,941 --> 00:30:16,653
Just as the president ordered.

521
00:30:16,653 --> 00:30:19,166
Are we gaining popularity
with the character lovers?

522
00:30:19,166 --> 00:30:21,361
Yeah, yeah, we're gaining.

523
00:30:21,361 --> 00:30:25,585
They're even calling you
the successor to Mondo-ism.

524
00:30:25,585 --> 00:30:26,973
What a relief.

525
00:30:26,973 --> 00:30:30,989
- Relief-ism!
- Relief-ism!

526
00:30:41,669 --> 00:30:44,289
Burn, burn.

527
00:30:44,289 --> 00:30:47,300
Flames, burn.

528
00:30:47,933 --> 00:30:50,489
We'll be resuming shortly.

529
00:30:58,925 --> 00:31:00,845
- Mr. Tokui.
- Yes?

530
00:31:00,845 --> 00:31:02,800
May I borrow a pen?

531
00:31:04,185 --> 00:31:06,466
- Go ahead.
- Thank you.

532
00:31:16,361 --> 00:31:17,730
[Cynical Molco]
The proposal competition

533
00:31:17,730 --> 00:31:19,100
[Final Proposal Competition]
is now starting!

534
00:31:21,033 --> 00:31:24,565
Here, suppose you've acquired
the rights to Cynical Molco.

535
00:31:24,565 --> 00:31:26,269
Please use an image board to show

536
00:31:26,269 --> 00:31:28,805
what kind of business development
you have in mind

537
00:31:28,805 --> 00:31:32,685
to Cynical Molco and to Mr. Omishima,

538
00:31:32,685 --> 00:31:36,545
in the form of a proposal competition.

539
00:31:38,701 --> 00:31:42,397
Are you drawing image boards, Mr. Seo?

540
00:31:42,397 --> 00:31:43,969
Yeah.

541
00:31:43,969 --> 00:31:48,917
I was thinking of making a collage,
so I'm collecting materials. But this one.

542
00:31:48,917 --> 00:31:51,037
Do you know it?

543
00:31:51,037 --> 00:31:57,005
It looks like Cynical Molco,
but it's kind of plain.

544
00:31:57,005 --> 00:32:01,505
And just like someone, it's kind of
unknown, not making a splash.

545
00:32:01,505 --> 00:32:04,393
- That's... That's...
- Huh? So you do know it?

546
00:32:04,393 --> 00:32:06,266
This 'unknown' one.

547
00:32:06,266 --> 00:32:12,500
Oh, wait. Why does the torn one look cuter?

548
00:32:15,977 --> 00:32:17,877
Mr. Seo is about to turn into
a wild beast, isn't he?

549
00:32:17,877 --> 00:32:19,905
Did Rena say something to him?

550
00:32:19,905 --> 00:32:21,649
Oh, come on.

551
00:32:33,637 --> 00:32:36,809
Molco rescue, Tuesla expo, O-Con marriage.

552
00:32:36,809 --> 00:32:39,421
Molco rescue, Tuesla expo, O-Con marriage.

553
00:32:39,421 --> 00:32:41,193
Molco rescue...

554
00:32:44,313 --> 00:32:49,413
That's Full Tummy Molco. Be nice to it.

555
00:32:53,077 --> 00:32:57,766
Why? The president said that
he had a short temper.

556
00:33:01,681 --> 00:33:05,905
[Time remaining]

557
00:33:05,905 --> 00:33:07,966
All right.

558
00:33:10,777 --> 00:33:12,249
Isn't that a bit too fast?

559
00:33:12,249 --> 00:33:13,539
If you're making something
with PowerPoint or AI,

560
00:33:13,539 --> 00:33:15,237
even in this amount of time...

561
00:33:15,237 --> 00:33:17,693
There's no need to rush.

562
00:33:17,693 --> 00:33:19,700
Everything is going as planned.

563
00:33:23,041 --> 00:33:27,005
Oh! Mr. Takarada is already proposing!

564
00:33:27,005 --> 00:33:28,861
[Teppei Takarada]
Please.

565
00:33:28,861 --> 00:33:32,593
Running and stuff? That kind of thing. Hmph.

566
00:33:33,625 --> 00:33:39,777
If you come to us, Molco,
what kind of future will come?

567
00:33:39,777 --> 00:33:44,466
Please listen to the story
of the future we've drawn.

568
00:33:45,625 --> 00:33:49,033
Molco and the Little Toy Shop.

569
00:34:04,125 --> 00:34:05,641
Molco rescue, Tuesla expo, O-Con marriage.

570
00:34:05,641 --> 00:34:07,301
Molco rescue, Tuesla expo, O-Con marriage.

571
00:34:07,301 --> 00:34:08,741
Molco rescue, Tuesla expo, O-Con marriage.

572
00:34:08,741 --> 00:34:11,000
Molco rescue, Tuesla expo, O-Con marriage.

573
00:34:14,033 --> 00:34:17,713
Huh? What was this character's name again?

574
00:34:17,713 --> 00:34:20,900
Ah, Mankitsu Mokugyo, right?

575
00:34:26,889 --> 00:34:29,161
If we can receive Molco's rights,

576
00:34:29,161 --> 00:34:33,353
we'll use our agency's methods
to the fullest,

577
00:34:33,353 --> 00:34:35,913
[Seigo Takamiya]
from jumbo passenger planes

578
00:34:35,913 --> 00:34:38,565
to giant urban visuals.

579
00:34:38,565 --> 00:34:42,589
We'll hijack the media's prime spots
and make them all about Molco.

580
00:34:42,589 --> 00:34:47,093
What was it again? Manmaru Monpe?

581
00:34:52,041 --> 00:34:54,281
Please look over there.

582
00:34:54,281 --> 00:34:55,617
[President and CEO]
The tens of thousands of

583
00:34:55,617 --> 00:34:56,957
[of Strada Logistics Co., Ltd.]
trucks running through town,

584
00:34:56,957 --> 00:34:59,349
[Eiji Kuramochi]
the uniforms, and the cardboard boxes.

585
00:34:59,349 --> 00:35:02,397
[Cynmor Logistics]
We'll fill everything with Molco.

586
00:35:02,397 --> 00:35:04,933
Mongol Turkey?

587
00:35:09,133 --> 00:35:11,333
Itoko to Hatoko?

588
00:35:23,525 --> 00:35:24,577
[People who put their all into
what they love are wonderful]

589
00:35:24,577 --> 00:35:25,673
[The prince looks happy.
He draws with such a nice expression.]

590
00:35:25,673 --> 00:35:27,393
[I can feel the love for the character.
He's most attractive when he's drawing.]

591
00:35:36,173 --> 00:35:39,900
[Time remaining]

592
00:35:41,213 --> 00:35:44,997
And now, there are only 30 minutes left.

593
00:35:44,997 --> 00:35:47,233
Hey, do you think he's okay?

594
00:35:50,461 --> 00:35:52,269
All right.

595
00:35:59,605 --> 00:36:02,105
[Kazuo Nimura]
Here comes Mr. Nimura of Peace Plus.

596
00:36:02,105 --> 00:36:03,941
Please.

597
00:36:05,561 --> 00:36:10,717
If you entrust Cynical Molco to Peace Plus,

598
00:36:10,717 --> 00:36:14,841
we'll invest a total budget of 30 billion yen

599
00:36:14,841 --> 00:36:19,701
and grow Molco into a global brand instantly.

600
00:36:19,701 --> 00:36:22,393
Movies, games, fashion,

601
00:36:22,393 --> 00:36:27,009
and amusement facilities like Molco Land.

602
00:36:27,009 --> 00:36:33,457
We'll establish all that worldwide
and expand Cynical Molco globally.

603
00:36:33,457 --> 00:36:38,057
Could you entrust us with
making this dream a reality?

604
00:36:38,057 --> 00:36:41,041
<i>Thank you. That was
an overwhelming presentation.</i>

605
00:36:41,041 --> 00:36:42,921
[Amazing! 30 billion yen!
Molco will become a world star!]

606
00:36:42,921 --> 00:36:47,037
And now, the remaining time is running out.

607
00:37:04,497 --> 00:37:08,157
Here comes Seo Design!

608
00:37:17,205 --> 00:37:19,113
Thank you.

609
00:37:22,497 --> 00:37:26,074
Mr. Seo, can you tell us about
your business development plan

610
00:37:26,074 --> 00:37:28,389
after acquiring Molco's rights?

611
00:37:29,037 --> 00:37:35,197
We will give up
the exclusive rights to Molco.

612
00:37:35,197 --> 00:37:37,057
What?

613
00:37:37,877 --> 00:37:40,566
I humbly cannot accept
what you have graciously given.

614
00:37:43,073 --> 00:37:46,657
What did that mean? Was that in the script?

615
00:37:46,657 --> 00:37:48,329
No, it wasn't.

616
00:37:48,329 --> 00:37:50,449
But it's okay.

617
00:37:50,449 --> 00:37:52,685
We practiced so much.

618
00:37:52,685 --> 00:37:56,185
So, Mr. Seo, what exactly...

619
00:37:57,353 --> 00:37:59,566
We, Seo Design.

620
00:38:02,305 --> 00:38:04,149
<i>We, Seo Design.</i>

621
00:38:04,149 --> 00:38:06,205
We, Seo Design.

622
00:38:06,205 --> 00:38:09,389
Will make the whole world
fall in love with Cynical Molco.

623
00:38:09,389 --> 00:38:13,233
Will make the whole world
fall in love with Cynical Molco.

624
00:38:13,233 --> 00:38:17,897
Will make the whole world
fall in love with Cynical Molco.

625
00:38:17,897 --> 00:38:19,159
[Making Molco]
We propose

626
00:38:19,159 --> 00:38:22,457
[Everyone's Property]
making Molco everyone's property.

627
00:38:22,457 --> 00:38:25,405
Make Molco everyone's property.

628
00:38:25,405 --> 00:38:27,781
- <i>Molco... To those who need Molco,</i>
- To those who need Molco,

629
00:38:27,781 --> 00:38:29,729
- <i>we'll open Molco up to everyone.</i>
- we'll open Molco up to everyone.

630
00:38:29,729 --> 00:38:33,277
It's as if Mr. Seo is
becoming like Ms. Kusakabe.

631
00:38:33,277 --> 00:38:36,589
Is this possession? Is he being
possessed by Ms. Kusakabe?

632
00:38:36,589 --> 00:38:40,333
And we won't be the rights holder,

633
00:38:41,597 --> 00:38:43,966
but the representative guardian.

634
00:38:46,105 --> 00:38:49,200
For example, if a hospital wants
to use Molco to comfort children

635
00:38:49,200 --> 00:38:51,693
who are afraid of hospitals,

636
00:38:51,693 --> 00:38:54,925
we'll allow them to use Molco freely

637
00:38:54,925 --> 00:38:57,581
on brochures, wall art, anything.

638
00:38:57,581 --> 00:39:00,831
Also, if a lackluster shopping district

639
00:39:00,831 --> 00:39:04,877
wants to use Molco as its image character
to liven things up,

640
00:39:04,877 --> 00:39:07,457
Molco will rush over.

641
00:39:07,457 --> 00:39:10,300
Of course, all that will be free of charge.

642
00:39:11,029 --> 00:39:13,741
Oh, then what about our place?

643
00:39:13,741 --> 00:39:17,717
Our visitors have decreased,
and the staff is all sad.

644
00:39:17,717 --> 00:39:19,881
Of course.

645
00:39:19,881 --> 00:39:22,673
If you want to use Molco's power
to make someone happy and joyful,

646
00:39:22,673 --> 00:39:28,529
if you want to borrow Molco's power,
we'll happily send Molco out to do that.

647
00:39:32,093 --> 00:39:38,057
However, I think there are also companies
that want to do business with Molco.

648
00:39:38,057 --> 00:39:44,573
In such cases, we'll ask Molco
to receive a salary.

649
00:39:45,589 --> 00:39:49,725
So that way, everyone's plans are feasible.

650
00:39:49,725 --> 00:39:50,765
[I want to ask for Molco to help with
our shop too! That's what I want!]

651
00:39:50,765 --> 00:39:51,773
[The love is so intense it makes me cry.
Seo's stock just skyrocketed.]

652
00:39:51,773 --> 00:39:53,433
[Molco can be a savior for
regional revitalization!]

653
00:39:53,433 --> 00:39:58,066
And among you all, there's this person.

654
00:40:08,357 --> 00:40:12,553
But in that case, Seo Design will ultimately

655
00:40:12,553 --> 00:40:18,253
monopolize the profits
while calling it Molco's salary, won't you?

656
00:40:18,253 --> 00:40:20,377
No.

657
00:40:20,377 --> 00:40:26,337
All salary that Molco receives
belongs only to Molco.

658
00:40:27,153 --> 00:40:29,129
It's not our company's profit.

659
00:40:29,129 --> 00:40:33,997
Instead, it will be used for
Molco's future growth.

660
00:40:33,997 --> 00:40:36,241
Consulting with everyone.

661
00:40:37,057 --> 00:40:39,117
<i>Molco becomes everyone's property.</i>

662
00:40:39,117 --> 00:40:44,057
The more people we have
who cherish Molco that much,

663
00:40:44,057 --> 00:40:49,733
the more we all protect
and nurture Molco together.

664
00:40:49,733 --> 00:40:53,453
That's the proposal from Seo Design.

665
00:40:53,453 --> 00:40:57,629
[Making Molco Everyone's Property]

666
00:40:57,629 --> 00:40:59,433
Interesting.

667
00:41:25,637 --> 00:41:27,761
I'm not convinced!

668
00:41:29,513 --> 00:41:35,017
I'm firmly against the idea of transferring

669
00:41:35,017 --> 00:41:39,100
Cynical Molco's rights to Seo Design!

670
00:41:40,369 --> 00:41:42,509
Everyone's property?

671
00:41:42,509 --> 00:41:46,845
I can't trust that kind of idealistic spin.

672
00:41:47,925 --> 00:41:52,566
Because Seo Design has Ms. Kusakabe.

673
00:41:53,805 --> 00:41:57,687
The problem is Anna Kusakabe,

674
00:41:57,687 --> 00:42:00,537
the consultant who's under contract
with Seo Design.

675
00:42:00,537 --> 00:42:01,917
Can you get her on camera?

676
00:42:01,917 --> 00:42:04,029
Yeah, the one in the gray jacket.

677
00:42:04,029 --> 00:42:05,389
Right, that's her.

678
00:42:05,389 --> 00:42:10,000
Everyone, are you familiar
with Kitchen Sakoda?

679
00:42:10,813 --> 00:42:16,733
It was Ms. Kusakabe's consulting that
made that restaurant a huge success.

680
00:42:16,733 --> 00:42:19,639
But it was also Ms. Kusakabe

681
00:42:19,639 --> 00:42:23,000
who drove the couple running
Kitchen Sakoda to divorce.

682
00:42:24,017 --> 00:42:26,481
Ignoring their wishes

683
00:42:26,481 --> 00:42:31,961
and driving a wedge between them
by prioritizing the numbers and money.

684
00:42:31,961 --> 00:42:34,200
Apparently, that's what caused the divorce.

685
00:42:35,773 --> 00:42:41,617
And I also have more information
that hasn't come to light yet.

686
00:42:42,341 --> 00:42:48,705
The remaining owner ran
the original Kitchen Sakoda alone.

687
00:42:48,705 --> 00:42:52,000
I heard it's closing due to poor performance.

688
00:42:53,049 --> 00:42:54,845
No way.

689
00:42:59,133 --> 00:43:00,157
[Not a consultant, just a homewrecker.]

690
00:43:00,157 --> 00:43:01,189
[Poor Kitchen Sakoda, targeted like that.]

691
00:43:01,189 --> 00:43:02,277
[Are Ms. Kusakabe's other clients okay?]

692
00:43:02,277 --> 00:43:03,909
[Could Seo be sweet-talked?
A divorce would ruin everything.]

693
00:43:03,909 --> 00:43:09,177
Ms. Kusakabe only cares
about money and numbers.

694
00:43:09,177 --> 00:43:13,066
I don't want Molco
anywhere near someone like that.

695
00:43:15,493 --> 00:43:21,166
She doesn't have any love for characters!

696
00:43:36,345 --> 00:43:39,689
Burn, burn.

697
00:43:40,461 --> 00:43:47,200
O-Con doesn't have any love for characters?

698
00:43:49,305 --> 00:43:50,749
Oh, my!

699
00:43:50,749 --> 00:43:53,453
<i>♪ Tuesla, Tutu-Tuesla ♪</i>

700
00:43:56,877 --> 00:43:58,705
Cute.

701
00:44:07,273 --> 00:44:10,389
Don't. Mr. Seo, don't!

702
00:44:23,997 --> 00:44:29,366
I'll never forgive anyone who hurts O-Con!
